From: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: install CoreSight SSDT (ETEs via Scope + sinks + funnel) for ACPI-booted CIX SKY1

CIX Orion O6 firmware boots Linux via ACPI. The CIXTEK SKY1EDK2 SSDT
already declares the 12 CPUs as ACPI0007 devices under
\_SB.C000.{C001..C005}.CPU{0..B}, but no CoreSight nodes are exposed.

Embed and dynamically install an SSDT that:
  - extends each existing CPU's namespace via Scope() to attach an
    ARMHC500 ETE child (no duplicate ACPI0007 declarations);
  - declares one ARMHC9FF dynamic SoC funnel (CSF0 @ 0x180B0000);
  - declares three ARMHC97C TMC ETFs (ETF0 @ 0x18060000,
    ETF1 @ 0x180A0000, ETF2 @ 0x19000000);
  - declares one ARMHC501 TMC ETR (ETR0 @ 0x180C0000).

The etm4x platform driver binds the ETEs via ACPI parent walk, and
the TMC/funnel ACPI platform drivers (patches 0009/0010) bind the
sinks and link.

STM (ARMHC502) and TRBE are intentionally absent; their drivers
need separate ACPI backports.

Signed-off-by: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
---
 src/drivers/acpi/Makefile         |   2 +
 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c | 179 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 181 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c

--- a/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/Makefile
@@ -133,2 +133,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_ACPI_VIOT)		+= viot.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_RISCV)		+= riscv/
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_ARCH_CIX)		+= sky1-coresight.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/drivers/acpi/sky1-coresight.c
@@ -0,0 +1,179 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * sky1-coresight: install a CoreSight SSDT at boot on CIX SKY1.
+ *
+ * Orion O6 firmware boots Linux via ACPI and declares the 12 CPUs as
+ * ACPI0007 devices under \_SB.C000.{C001..C005}.CPU{0..B} (CIXTEK
+ * SKY1EDK2 SSDT). It does NOT expose any CoreSight nodes. This driver
+ * installs an additional SSDT that uses Scope() to attach an ARMHC500
+ * ETE child to each existing CPU, plus standalone ARMHC9FF dynamic
+ * funnel, three ARMHC97C TMC ETF sinks and one ARMHC501 TMC ETR sink.
+ *
+ * STM (ARMHC502) and TRBE are not declared here; their drivers in
+ * 6.6.x lack ACPI match tables and need separate backports.
+ */
